  explosively but it's not as efficient as  just adding extra weight and now you  need to recruit more muscle fiber in  order to be more explosive more fast  twitch muscle fiber in order to generate  more power through that movement through  the exact same movement then when you go  back to that movement and train without  the weighted vest you'll find that you  can much more easily launch yourself up  to the Year you almost can't help  yourself from flying up straight past  the bar krisily pull-ups are one example  but there's loads of other exercises  that are well suited to this pretty much  any calisthenics so things like crawls  things like push-ups  press ups clapping press ups things like  squats air squats pistol squats which  are also extra difficult because you now  got your weight  mind you all kinds of things can be made  more difficult by wearing a weighted  vest  studies show that performing jumps with  a weighted vest will increase your jump  height which is no surprise because once  again you're recruiting more muscle  fiber more faster to muscle fiber  through the exact same technique these  studies are very limited though one  often quoted study looking at the effect  of weighted vests on jump height family  effect was actually extremely minor and  that there was no noticeable change in  women weirdly well the most notable  change was observed was in the initial  pre-take-off velocity how quickly the  participants were able to drive their  bodies through the ground to launch  upwards that makes a lot of sense given  that the vest would help them to recruit  more muscle fiber more quickly as they  made this movement it's just that this  small difference didn't translate to  massive gains in jump height the study  has a lot of methodological problems  though for instance I only had 18  participants who are all recruited from  a college and they were not given nearly  enough time to train in order to see  long-term results the study only looked  at im