ougher they should be go  ahead and act like Goku or piccolo and  wear weighted clothing all the time  unfortunately not there are a couple of  limitations the first one is they're  having a lot of weight on your shoulders  in particular can put a lot of strain on  your body like quite doing things like  explosive jumping is going to look put a  lot of impact on your knees and that  could be bad for you of course you need  to be careful you need to limit the  amount you're doing you certainly need  to build up to it I'd recommend not  using too much weight to begin with that  fifth  percent is a really good option actually  and you'll find that you don't need much  more than that when you're first  starting out I certainly don't you  always have the option of making the  move slightly more difficult rather than  adding more weight there are some ways  you can mitigate this for instance some  weighted vests try to take some of the  weight off your shoulders and put it  across your waist but it's still an  awful lot of strain on the body so I  wouldn't recommend doing this all day  every day plus you get really hot  it chafes you just beat yourself up  basically the other problem with this is  that wearing weighted vest all day would  change your center of gravity and that  would potentially alter the way that  your brain thinks about your body or get  too used to moving with the weights so  that it would become less efficient at  moving without the weight so you might  struggle with things like balance your  body has learned to balance with your  weight over countless years of practice  if you suddenly put more weight on top  than down below you're gonna mess that  up a little bit if the weight was  perfectly distributed across your body  that might be a different story but no  piece of equipment can accomplish quite  that unless I go into a gravity route  that said it is a really cool concept if  you'd like to see me attempt to go a  whole day or a couple of days we